<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 2.6 pct in December -Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 2.6 pct in December -Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   Dec 96     Nov 96   (Dec 95)</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.1	  0.3	(0.2)</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     2.6	  2.6	(5.8)</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    104.9	104.8    (116.7)</p>
<p>Note: The 1996 data is based on a new basket of goods. The 1995 data was collated under an old basket.</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 2.7 percent for November.  </p>
<p>Note: Istat said average inflation for 1996 was 3.9 percent against 5.4 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     104.6	    0.0	    2.8</p>
<p> Clothing			 105.9	   +0.2	    3.3</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   107.0	   +0.1	    4.7</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 104.8	    0.0	    2.3</p>
<p> Health spending		102.7	    0.0	    2.0</p>
<p> Transport			105.9	   +0.2	    2.2</p>
<p> Recreation		     103.7	   +0.1	    2.1</p>
<p> Education			107.2	   +0.2	    2.4</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  104.9	    0.0	    3.2</p>
<p> Other goods,service	  103.1	   +0.1	    1.2</p>
<p>(including communications)</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
